# The paraxial equation is exact only for waves at the reference index. A mode of index n shows n0 + (n^2 - n0^2) / (2 n0) instead.
# Reference: that formula applied to the mode of the transverse grid, with the phase per step t replaced by 2 atan(t / 2) as the Crank-Nicolson step does.
title Straight guide with the reference index set to 1.444
window width=12 length=100
reference 1.444
guide straight x=0 width=0.5 from=0 to=100
launch mode x=0 width=0.5
monitor out z=100 x=0 width=0.5
plane end z=100
expect power out 0.999998912 2e-7
expect total end 0.999999494 2e-7
expect centroid end 0.0000000 2e-6
expect radius end 0.2753119 2e-6
expect neff 2.830676566 2e-8
expect neff 2.83067657 2e-6
expect power_above out 0.9995
